    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d800">

                <pb facs="0904" n="819" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg819"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.48/1144: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d800-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic">January 16,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>4095. The American Committee for Armenian and Syrian Belief are sending three
                    ships to Turkey: The United States Naval Transport <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mercurius</hi> now ready to sail with five members of the relief expedition
                    and carries cargo for Constantinople only; the United States Naval Transport <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Pensacola</hi> with between 30 and 40 members of the
                    relief expedition and a cargo of supplies to be discharged partly at Beirut and
                    partly at Constantinople, sailing about January 21; and the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Western Belle</hi> sailing shortly from New York with
                        <pb facs="0905" n="820" xml:id="pg820"/> a cargo of approximately 8,000 tons
                    of flour, to be discharged at Constantinople and possibly Beirut. Before
                    authorizing these vessels to sail from the United States, the Naval Overseas
                    Transportation Service desires to have full assurance that these vessels will
                    encounter no obstacles in passing the Dardanelles and entering the port of
                    Constantinople and also that the <hi rendition="#italic">Pensacola</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Western Belle</hi>, if so ordered, will be able to enter
                    the port of Beirut. Inasmuch as one vessel is now ready to sail, immediate reply
                    is requested. Repeat to Paris as number 6997.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d800-f1" n="16" type="source" xml:id="d800-f1-content">
                <p>See last sentence for instructions to repeat to Paris No. 6997.</p>
